<Base title="about — TinkSoft">
    <h1>about</h1>
    <p>Hi, I'm Tink. TinkSoft is where I build software in public.</p>
    <p>
        Building in public means sharing the whole process, the bugs that ate
        away at the subprocesses of my mind, the architecture decisions I know I
        will regret in six months. Writing it down keeps me excited and keeps me
        working. It also serves to show what a novice wizard like me can
        accomplish today with AI.
    </p>
    <p>
        Every post in the <a href="/">build log</a> is a real update from a real project.
        No polish, no marketing. Just what happened.
    </p>
    <h2>why the 90s look?</h2>
    <p>
        Because the old web was fast, honest, and built by people making things
        for the fun of it. This site is plain HTML, ships zero JavaScript, and
        loads instantly on anything. That felt right.
    </p>
    <h2>link to me</h2>
    <p>
        <img
            src="/badge.svg"
            width="88"
            height="31"
            alt="TINKSOFT 88x31 button"
        />
        — a classic 88&times;31 button, like the old web intended. Grab it:
    </p>
    <div class="content">
        <pre>&lt;a href="https://tinksoft.com"&gt;&lt;img
  src="https://tinksoft.com/badge.svg"
  width="88" height="31" alt="TINKSOFT"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</pre>
    </div>
    <h2>get in touch</h2>
    <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:tinkxiu@gmail.com">tinkxiu@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
</Base>
